# Docker build context for the native C++ build (docker/build.Dockerfile).
#
# The repo is ~2.8 GB on disk. The two monsters are:
#   content/art          1.2 GB   (authored art / Kenney packs)
#   .claude/worktrees    1.6 GB   (parallel agent checkouts, nested inside the repo)
# Neither is needed to COMPILE. The C++ build needs source, CMake files and
# nothing else; content/ is read at RUNTIME by the natively-run binary straight
# out of the repo, so it never has to enter the build context.
#
# This file is therefore an ALLOWLIST: deny everything, then re-admit the few
# directories the compiler actually reads. That keeps the context in the low
# hundreds of KB and, more importantly, keeps it that way when someone drops
# another gigabyte of art into the tree.

**

# --- re-admitted: the only things the build actually compiles ---
!native/**
!docker/**

# --- and then trim build junk back out of the re-admitted paths ---
native/build/**
native/out/**
native/.cache/**
native/**/*.o
native/**/*.obj
native/**/*.exe
native/**/*.pdb
native/**/*.ilk
native/**/CMakeUserPresets.json
native/**/.DS_Store
